claims.text:
1. A laminate composed of at least two metal sheets having a synthetic layer bonded therebetween, said layer containing continuous glass filaments wherein:
A) the glass filaments have a modulus of elasticity of 80–100 GPa;
B) the metal sheets each have a thickness of less than 1.5 mm and contain a material having a tensile strength greater than 0.20 GPa;
C) the metal sheets are of a metal selected from the group consisting of: aluminum alloys; steel; titanium alloys; copper; copper alloys and magnesium alloys; and
D) the glass filaments extend parallel to each other in at least one direction; constitute 35–75% by volume of the synthetic layer; and are comprised of 58–69% by weight of SiO_{2} and 18–29% by weight of Al_{2}O_{3}.
